The module loader validates section contents and names before calling
module_frob_arch_sections(), but it does not validate the sh_info target
index of SHT_REL and SHT_RELA sections. The ARM, ARM64, LoongArch,
PA-RISC and RISC-V hooks use this index before apply_relocations() skips
out-of-range indices.

On ARM with ARM_MODULE_PLTS, an out-of-range index reads sh_flags from a
section header outside the table. The ARM32 A/B test reported "Unable to
handle kernel paging request" in the hook. PA-RISC uses the index for an
e_shnum-sized heap array when a relocation needs a stub. Its A/B test
produced a Data TLB miss on the out-of-bounds stub_entries read before
reaching the update. ARM64, LoongArch and RISC-V contain the same early
section-header read.

Reject relocation sections whose target index is outside the section
table during the early ELF validity pass. This checks the shared ELF
invariant before any architecture hook runs.

Fixes: c298be74492b ("parisc: fix module loading failure of large kernel modules")
Fixes: 7d485f647c1f ("ARM: 8220/1: allow modules outside of bl range")
Fixes: fd045f6cd98e ("arm64: add support for module PLTs")
Fixes: ab1ef68e5401 ("RISC-V: Add sections of PLT and GOT for kernel module")
Fixes: fcdfe9d22bed ("LoongArch: Add ELF and module support")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Karl Mehltretter <kmehltretter@gmail.com>
---

Analysis and testing:

At Linux b9b3e33b70b7 ("Merge tag 'trace-v7.2-rc6' of
git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/trace/linux-trace"), a
custom Fragma harness used upstream Frama-C 33.0 (Arsenic) Eva to
analyze a source-identical ARM module_frob_arch_sections() slice. Eva
reported the out-of-range section-table pointer and sh_flags access.

ARM32 A/B testing at b9b3e33b70b7 used QEMU 10.2.1 virt/TCG with a
Cortex-A15 CPU, GCC 15.2.0, and multi_v7_defconfig plus VMSPLIT_2G. The
control module loaded and unloaded on both kernels. With only a SHT_REL
sh_info field changed from 10 to 0x10000000, the original kernel faulted
at module_frob_arch_sections()+0x160. The fixed kernel rejected the same
module with ENOEXEC and the invalid-index diagnostic.

PA-RISC A/B testing at the base commit used QEMU 10.2.1 B160L/TCG,
hppa-linux-gcc 8.1.0, binutils 2.30, and generic-32bit_defconfig. The
control module loaded and unloaded on both byte-identically configured
kernels. With only a SHT_RELA sh_info field changed from 3 to 0x10000000
in a section containing a counted R_PARISC_PCREL17F relocation, the
original kernel produced a Data TLB miss at
module_frob_arch_sections()+0x11c. Disassembly identifies the faulting
instruction as the stub_entries read used by WARN_ON(). The later store
was not reached. The fixed kernel rejected the same module with ENOEXEC
and printed target index 268435456.

The fixed tree also completed full vmlinux builds for ARM64 defconfig
with GCC 15.2.0, RISC-V defconfig plus RELOCATABLE with GCC 15.2.0, and
LoongArch loongson64_defconfig with LLVM 21.1.8. MODULE_SECTIONS was
enabled for RISC-V. These were build-only checks. No physical hardware
was tested.
---
 kernel/module/main.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/module/main.c b/kernel/module/main.c
index d0e1e0bd2ad0..30c7a05488bc 100644
--- a/kernel/module/main.c
+++ b/kernel/module/main.c
@@ -1933,6 +1933,7 @@ static int elf_validity_ehdr(const struct load_info *info)
  * * Section array fits in the user provided data
  * * Section index 0 is NULL
  * * Section contents are inbounds
+ * * Relocation section target indices are inbounds
  *
  * Then updates @info with a &load_info->sechdrs pointer if valid.
  *
@@ -1983,6 +1984,12 @@ static int elf_validity_cache_sechdrs(struct load_info *info)
 	/* Validate contents are inbounds */
 	for (i = 1; i < info->hdr->e_shnum; i++) {
 		shdr = &sechdrs[i];
+		if ((shdr->sh_type == SHT_REL || shdr->sh_type == SHT_RELA) &&
+		    shdr->sh_info >= info->hdr->e_shnum) {
+			pr_err("Invalid ELF relocation section target index %u\n",
+			       shdr->sh_info);
+			return -ENOEXEC;
+		}
 		switch (shdr->sh_type) {
 		case SHT_NULL:
 		case SHT_NOBITS:

